LOCAL MODIFICATIONS
-------------------
None. The copy here is unmodified upstream source. Orbit uses Trixnity through its
published Maven artifacts, not from this folder; this tree is read-only reference
material.

A second, near-identical copy used to live at `trixnity_sources/`. It differed from
this tree by one modified condition in MatrixClient.kt, which inverted the guard
while leaving its own error message unchanged:

    require(newUserId != userId || newDeviceId != deviceId) {
        "...must match stored authenticated userId ..."

The condition required the two ids to DIFFER while the message said they must match.
Neither folder is compiled -- only `:webrtc-java-lib` is a real Gradle module -- so
this was never in a shipped binary, but a reference tree that contradicts its own
message is worse than no reference tree. The modified copy was removed rather than
corrected, since the unmodified upstream text is the correct one.
